sequenceDiagram
  actor U as Human
  participant C as Native connector<br/>Gateway
  box rgb(237,243,248) Control plane process
    participant O as OCC<br/>IAM and State unit
  end
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant H as Actual Harness<br/>Agent runtime
  participant K as Credential owner
  participant R as Protected model<br/>repository receivers

  Note over U,R: 1 · Enroll and grant exact access
  U->>O: Administrator enrolls human, then explicit grants
  O->>D: Original transaction and complete lock order
  D-->>O: Committed receipt or uncertain COMMIT
  O-->>U: Recoverable policy outcome
  Note over O,D: Uncertain COMMIT remains unknown.<br/>No replay or destructive compensation.

  Note over U,R: 2 · Admit a native request
  U->>C: Requester B sends personal DM or team mention
  C->>O: Verified event, sender and original reply handle
  O->>O: Current account, context, invoke and baseline
  alt Missing or stale authority
    O-->>C: Denied or unavailable
    Note over C,H: Failed admission blocks default dispatch.
  else Current authority
    O->>D: Commit invocation, authority, audit and dispatch fence
    D-->>O: Durable admission
    O-->>C: Original invocation identity

  Note over U,R: 3 · Prepare exact protected execution
  O->>H: Select usable execution and observe actual incarnation
  H-->>O: Exact observed execution
  O->>O: Bind immutable delivery attempt
  O->>K: Open registered session and read back exact material
  K-->>O: Original admitted session
  O->>H: Deliver material bound to observed incarnation
  H->>R: Protected probe from actual execution
  R-->>O: Receiving evidence for current-serving selection
  O->>O: Select current serving after required evidence
  Note over O,R: Existing usable execution can be reused.<br/>Original authority and session horizons remain fixed.

  Note over U,R: 4 · Dispatch once and use admitted authority
  O->>H: Dispatch original admitted turn
  H-->>O: Runtime turn reference or unknown start
  O->>D: Retain turn or uncertainty
  Note over O,H: Unknown start cannot authorize redispatch.<br/>Only the actual admitted turn continues.
  H->>R: Model or git-read operation for original requester
  R->>R: Verify actual request and current authority
  R-->>H: Protected operation result
  H-->>O: Runtime result reference

  Note over U,R: 5 · Disclose to the authorized audience
  O->>O: Recheck content, full audience and original reply authority
  O->>D: Retain separate native submission fence
  D-->>O: Original eligible submission
  O->>C: Authorized result and original handle
  C-->>U: Native response
  C->>O: Confirmed, failed or unknown send
  O->>D: Retain outcome and late observations
  Note over C,D: Unknown send never permits resend.<br/>Late observations cannot reopen eligibility.

  end

  Note over U,R: 6 · Withdraw affected authority
  U->>O: Authorized narrowing change
  O->>D: Commit narrowing and refuse new work/results
  O->>K: Close affected sessions after committed narrowing
  O->>R: Protective traffic closure survives permission loss
  O->>H: Cancel affected work or stop exact revision
  R-->>O: Traffic closure evidence
  H-->>O: Observed stop or unresolved termination
  Note over O,R: Measure new-work refusal and last protected bytes within 30 seconds.<br/>Scoped five-second ceilings remain stricter.<br/>Physical stop and provider cleanup are separate outcomes.
  Note over U,R: Entire lifecycle proposed and unqualified.<br/>Time flows downward. Solid arrows request. Dashed arrows reply.
